<div class="rn">
<h2>What&#x27;s New in 6.1</h2>
<h3 class="hl">Highlights</h3>
<ul class="highlights">
<li><strong>OpenCode in the Quota Meter.</strong> Running OpenCode sessions now appear under the OpenCode logo, below Codex and Claude, each marked working or idle. Limits and burn rate are not there yet. OpenCode Go users who want to help add them: <a href="https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/issues">open an issue</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Improvements</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Better crash reports.</strong> A crash report you choose to send now includes the exception message and where it was thrown, so crashes that showed only system frames can be fixed.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Live sessions keep their own title.</strong> An agent started in a folder inside your home folder or a temp folder, with no conversation yet, could show the title of an old session started in that parent folder.</li>
</ul>
<p class="more">Full release notes: <a href="https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/releases/tag/v6.1">https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/releases/tag/v6.1</a></p>
</div>
